<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0001371> rdfs:label "Flexion contracture"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "A flexion contracture is a bent (flexed) joint that cannot be straightened actively or passively. It is thus a chronic loss of joint motion due to structural changes in muscle, tendons, ligaments, or skin that prevents normal movement of joints." ;
